<title>USA: TENNIS-SEEDINGS FOR THE U.S. OPEN CHAMPIONSHIP.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-SEEDINGS FOR THE U.S. OPEN CHAMPIONSHIP.</headline>
<dateline>WHITE PLAINS, New York 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seedings for the</p>
<p>U.S. Open tennis championships starting next Monday, as issued</p>
<p>by the U.S. Tennis Association on Tuesday:</p>
<p>Men's seedings</p>
<p>1. Pete Sampras (U.S.)</p>
<p>2. Michael Chang (U.S.)</p>
<p>3. Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia)</p>
<p>4. Goran Ivanisevic (Croatia)</p>
<p>5. Thomas Muster (Austria)</p>
<p>6. Alex Corretja (Spain)</p>
<p>7. Sergi Brugera (Spain)</p>
<p>8. Carlos Moya (Spain)</p>
<p>9. Gustavo Kuerten (Brazil)</p>
<p>10. Marcelo Rios (Chile)</p>
<p>11. Thomas Enqvist (Sweden)</p>
<p>12. Felix Mantilla (Spain)</p>
<p>13. Boris Becker (Germany)</p>
<p>14. Patrick Rafter (Australia)</p>
<p>15. Mark Philippoussis (Australia)</p>
<p>16. Petr Korda (Czech Republic)</p>
<p>Women's seedings</p>
<p>1. Martina Hingis (Switzerland)</p>
<p>2. Monica Seles (U.S.)</p>
<p>3. Jana Novotna (Czech Republic)</p>
<p>4. Iva Majoli (Croatia)</p>
<p>5. Amanda Coetzer (South Africa)</p>
<p>6. Lindsay Davenport (U.S.)</p>
<p>7. Conchita Martinez (Spain)</p>
<p>8. Anke Huber (Germany)</p>
<p>9. Mary Pierce (France)</p>
<p>10. Arantxa Sanchez Vicario (Spain)</p>
<p>11. Irina Spirlea (Romania)</p>
<p>12. Mary Joe Fernandez (U.S.)</p>
<p>13. Brenda Schultz-McCarthy (Netherlands)</p>
<p>14. Barbara Paulus (Austria)</p>
<p>15. Ruxandra Dragomir (Romania)</p>
<p>16. Kim Po (U.S.)</p>
</text>
